{
 "protocol": "Pick TRAIN Zelda windows that match the judged held-out blur windows (experiments/blur_samples/windows.json) in\nfilter and scene, so blur on frames the dynamics model trained on can be compared with blur on held-out frames.\n\nWindows: context start, +4, +8, target +12 (context 3, frame_skip 4), inside one contiguous train segment, train rows\n>= 1000 (the dynamics loader skips the first 1000). Stride 4 as the held-out set, every start (stride 1) in the house rows.\nFilter (as the held-out set): camera still (phase-correlation shift of the target vs the last context frame = (0, 0)) and\n64..2048 moving pixels (evaluation.motion.moving_token_mask, patch 1, thr 0.1); box = the 32x32 box with most moving px.\nScene: nearest judged held-out window by RMSE of the 32x32 average-pooled target frames (RGB in [0, 1]); a train window\nis \"like block b\" when its nearest judged window is in block b at RMSE <= --radius, \"outdoor/other\" when every judged\nwindow is farther than --far.\nSelection: every eligible window in the house train rows (--house), then evenly spaced picks among the windows like\nblocks 1, 5 and 2-3 (quotas below), then evenly spaced \"other\" windows over the video.\n\n    python experiments/train_blur/select_windows.py --out experiments/train_blur/train_windows.json\n",
